# Environment Configuration Template

This file provides a template for environment variables used by the fantasy-baseball-player service.

## Usage

Copy this file to `.env` in the project root and update with your values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your configuration
```

The `.env` file is used by Docker Compose to inject environment variables into containers.

## Configuration Variables

### ASP.NET Core Settings

```bash
# ASP.NET Core runtime URLs
# Default: http://+:8080
ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:8080

# ASP.NET Core environment (Development/Staging/Production)
# Default: Production
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production

# Enable/disable detailed error messages
# Default: false
ASPNETCORE_DETAILEDLOG=false
```

### Player Database Configuration

```bash
# Database name
PLAYER_DATABASE=player_database

# Database hostname/IP
# In Docker Compose: use service name 'database'
# In production: use actual database server
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=database

# Database port
# Default: 5432
PLAYER_DATABASE_PORT=5432

# Database user
PLAYER_DATABASE_USER=postgres

# Database password
# WARNING: This is for development only. Use secrets management in production.
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=postgres

# Connection pool configuration
# Max connections: Default 20
# PLAYER_DATABASE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=20
```

### Position Service Integration

```bash
# Position Service hostname/IP
# Used for health checks and player-position mapping
POSITION_SERVICE_HOST=mountebank

# Position Service port
# Default: 5555
POSITION_SERVICE_PORT=5555

# Position Service version endpoint
POSITION_SERVICE_VERSION=v1

# Position Service timeout (seconds)
# Default: 10
POSITION_SERVICE_TIMEOUT=10
```

### Logging Configuration

```bash
# Log level (Debug/Information/Warning/Error/Critical)
# Default: Information
LOG_LEVEL=Information

# Log to console
LOG_TO_CONSOLE=true

# Log to file
# LOG_TO_FILE=true
# LOG_FILE_PATH=/var/log/fantasy-baseball-player/

# Detailed logging for database queries
# Default: false (disable in production)
LOG_DATABASE_QUERIES=false
```

### Health Check Configuration

```bash
# Health check enabled
# Default: true
HEALTH_CHECK_ENABLED=true

# Health check interval (seconds)
HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL=30

# Database health check timeout (seconds)
DATABASE_HEALTH_CHECK_TIMEOUT=10

# Position Service health check timeout (seconds)
POSITION_SERVICE_HEALTH_CHECK_TIMEOUT=10
```

### CORS Configuration

```bash
# Allowed origins for CORS requests
# Comma-separated list
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:8080,https://app.example.com

# Allow credentials in CORS requests
CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS=true

# Allowed HTTP methods
CORS_ALLOWED_METHODS=GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS

# Allowed headers
CORS_ALLOWED_HEADERS=Content-Type,Authorization
```

### Application Features

```bash
# Enable API documentation (Swagger)
ENABLE_SWAGGER=true

# CSV export enabled
ENABLE_CSV_EXPORT=true

# Projection data merge enabled
ENABLE_PROJECTION_MERGE=true
```

### Performance Tuning

```bash
# Request timeout (seconds)
REQUEST_TIMEOUT=30

# Database query timeout (seconds)
DATABASE_QUERY_TIMEOUT=30

# Connection pool size
# Default: 20
CONNECTION_POOL_SIZE=20

# Cache enabled
CACHE_ENABLED=false
```

### Security Settings

```bash
# API key authentication enabled
API_KEY_ENABLED=false

# API key (if authentication enabled)
# API_KEY=your-secret-api-key

# HTTPS redirect
# Default: false for development
HTTPS_REDIRECT=false

# HSTS enabled
# Default: false for development
HSTS_ENABLED=false

# HSTS max age (seconds)
# Default: 31536000 (1 year)
HSTS_MAX_AGE=31536000
```

### Development Settings

```bash
# Development mode enables detailed error messages
# NEVER use in production
# Default: false
DEVELOPMENT_MODE=false

# Mock Position Service responses (for testing without actual service)
MOCK_POSITION_SERVICE=false

# Use in-memory database (for testing)
USE_INMEMORY_DATABASE=false
```

## Configuration Examples

### Local Development

```bash
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=localhost
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=postgres
POSITION_SERVICE_HOST=localhost
LOG_LEVEL=Debug
LOG_DATABASE_QUERIES=true
ENABLE_SWAGGER=true
```

### Docker Compose Development

```bash
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=database
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=postgres
POSITION_SERVICE_HOST=mountebank
LOG_LEVEL=Information
ENABLE_SWAGGER=true
```

### Production

```bash
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=db.production.internal
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=${SECURE_PASSWORD}  # Use secrets management
POSITION_SERVICE_HOST=position-service.production
LOG_LEVEL=Warning
ENABLE_SWAGGER=false
HTTPS_REDIRECT=true
HSTS_ENABLED=true
```

### Staging/Testing

```bash
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Staging
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=db.staging.internal
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=${STAGING_PASSWORD}
POSITION_SERVICE_HOST=position-service.staging
LOG_LEVEL=Information
ENABLE_SWAGGER=true
```

## Security Best Practices

### Never Commit Secrets

```bash
# ✅ DO: Use environment variables or secrets management
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=${DB_PASSWORD}

# ❌ DON'T: Hardcode secrets in .env
PLAYER_DATABASE_PASSWORD=actual_password
```

### Use Secrets Management in Production

```bash
# Use Docker secrets (Docker Swarm)
# Use Kubernetes secrets (Kubernetes)
# Use cloud provider secrets (AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, etc.)
# Use HashiCorp Vault or similar
```

### Rotate Credentials

- Rotate database passwords every 90 days
- Rotate API keys on a regular schedule
- Immediately rotate if compromised

### Network Security

```bash
# Production database should NOT be exposed directly
# Use private networks and VPN
PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST=db.internal  # Private network only

# HTTPS required in production
HTTPS_REDIRECT=true
HSTS_ENABLED=true
```

## Troubleshooting Configuration

### Variable Not Being Applied

1. Ensure Docker Compose is using the .env file:
   ```bash
   docker compose config | grep -A 20 'environment:'
   ```

2. Restart containers for changes to take effect:
   ```bash
   docker compose down
   docker compose up -d
   ```

### Database Connection Failed

1. Verify database hostname and credentials:
   ```bash
   docker compose exec api pg_isready -h ${PLAYER_DATABASE_HOST} -U ${PLAYER_DATABASE_USER}
   ```

2. Check firewall/network:
   ```bash
   docker network ls
   docker network inspect fantasy-baseball-player_default
   ```

### Position Service Unreachable

1. Verify Position Service is running:
   ```bash
   curl http://${POSITION_SERVICE_HOST}:${POSITION_SERVICE_PORT}/api/health
   ```

2. Check network connectivity:
   ```bash
   docker compose exec api ping ${POSITION_SERVICE_HOST}
   ```

